        "node_id": "n_1_ad7b0d",
        "thought_text": "Consider the geometric interpretation where A and B are points on a number line, and K is the point equidistant from both A and B. This suggests that K could be the midpoint of A and B.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1791451372.8421
      },
      "rev_n_2_3ab4c6_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_3ab4c6_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_3ab4c6",
        "thought_text": "Explore the algebraic manipulation of the equation |A - K| = |B - K|. By squaring both sides, we might eliminate the absolute values and solve for K.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1791451372.84215
      },
      "rev_n_3_f8571d_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_f8571d_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_f8571d",
        "thought_text": "Since A and B are distinct, there exists a unique value of K that minimizes the sum of distances from K to A and B. This could be related to the concept of a median in statistics.",
